{\up >}{\footnote\pard\plain{\up >} main}
\pard\keepn\tx355 \b\fs36\cf1 Principal Operation
\par \pard\tx355 \plain\fs24 
\par \trowd\trgaph105\trleft-116 \cellx5665\cellx13255\pard\intbl \b 
\par\intbl 1\plain\fs24  Left joystick to control \b X/Y \plain\fs24 and \b Rotation 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl 2 \plain\fs24 Controller housing
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl \b 3\plain\fs24  Right joystick to control \b Z\plain\fs24  and \b Tilt 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl 4 \plain\fs24 Position display for X, Y, Z in mm, T and R in degrees.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl The travel speed is increased when the joystick is moved further from its centre position. 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl Releasing the joystick stops the stage movement.
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl The movements of the stage are \b magnification compensated\plain\fs24 . This means that if you select low magnification, the stage will travel large distances fast and at high magnification the travel will be small. 
\par\intbl 
\par\intbl Also, stage movements are\b  rotation compensated\plain\fs24 , that is even if the scan is rotated, the movement in X will still be horizontal and the movement in Y will be vertical.\b \par\pard \pard\intbl\li845 \plain\fs22 \cell\pard \pard\intbl\li845 \pard\intbl \fs24 \{bmc bm5.wmf\}\cell\intbl\row
\pard 
\par \page
